Package: es4all
Type: Package
Title: Effect Sizes for All Data Types with CI's and P-Values
Version: 0.9.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "[REDACTED]"
        , family = "[REDACTED]"
        , role = c("aut", "cre")
        , email = "REDACTED@example.com"
        , comment = c(ORCID = "[REDACTED]") )
Description: Effect sizes for all variable types: continuous, binary, and
    ordinal. Clear explanations to convey the practical significance of
    differences to both statistical and non-statistical audiences. Text snippets
    that authors can directly incorporate into the Methods and Results sections
    of their research papers. Promote transparent and accessible communication
    of empirical findings while fostering evidence-based decision making across
    disciplines. Includes common language effect size, generalized odds ratio, 
    Cliff's delta, Vargha and Delaney's A, Goodman and Kruskal's gamma, and
    other dominance-based effect sizes. Confidence intervals and p-values /
    hypothesis tests. 
